✅ 3.Thread Lifecycle

After:
thread.start();

Thread moves through states:

NEW
 | start()
 ▼
RUNNABLE
 | Selected by Thread Scheduler
 ▼
(Running - Conceptual)
 | wait(), join(), park()
 ▼
WAITING
 | notify(), notifyAll(), interrupt()
 ▼
RUNNABLE
 | sleep(), wait(timeout), join(timeout)
 ▼
TIMED_WAITING
 | timeout expires
 ▼
RUNNABLE
 | synchronized lock unavailable
 ▼
BLOCKED
 | lock acquired
 ▼
RUNNABLE
 | run() completes
 ▼
TERMINATED

Explanation of Each State

🔴 NEW → The Thread object is created using new but start() has not been called yet.
🔴 RUNNABLE → After start() is called, the thread is ready to run and is waiting for CPU time from the Thread Scheduler.
🔴 BLOCKED → Waiting to acquire a monitor lock (synchronized).
🔴 WAITING → Waiting indefinitely for another thread to perform an action (wait(), join(), park()).
🔴 TIMED_WAITING → Waiting for a specified time (sleep(), wait(timeout), join(timeout)).
🔴 RUNNING → The scheduler selects the thread, and the run() method starts executing.
🔴 TERMINATED → The run() method completes or exits due to an uncaught exception.The thread's execution is finished and it cannot be restarted.